data.content:
Here are the two files:

**`SortableList.razor`** — the template with Move Up/Down buttons per item.  
**`SortableList.razor.cs`** — the `partial class` code-behind.

Key design points:

- **Generic** (`@typeparam TItem`) — works with any item type.
- **Immutable input** — `Items` parameter is `IReadOnlyList<TItem>`, copied to a private `_items` list in `OnParametersSet` (never mutates the parent's list).
- **EventCallback** — after each swap, fires `OnOrderChanged` with a read-only copy of the reordered list.
- **`@key`** — ensures efficient diffing when items move.

Usage matches your example (with `ItemTemplate` as the template parameter name):

```razor
<SortableList Items="@tasks" OnOrderChanged="HandleReorder">
    <ItemTemplate>
        <span>@context.Title</span>
    </ItemTemplate>
</SortableList>

@code {
    private List<TaskItem> tasks = [ /* ... */ ];

    private void HandleReorder(IReadOnlyList<TaskItem> updated)
    {
        tasks = updated.ToList();
    }
}
```
